<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australia 97/98 weat may be 17.8 mln tonnes - USDA.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australia 97/98 weat may be 17.8 mln tonnes - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia may harvest 17.8 million tonnes of wheat in 1997/98, a sizable drop from this year's bumper crop, the U.S. agricultural attache in Canberra said in a report released Friday.</p>
<p>The attache, in an annual report on Australian crops, said wheat sowings were expected to drop in 1997/98 to 10.5 million hectares due to lower prices and land rotation plans.</p>
<p>The Australian Bureau of Agriculture and Resource Economics has estimated the 1996/97 crop at a record 23.497 million tonnes from 11 million hectares. U.S. Agriculture Department has pegged the crop at 23.1 million tonnes.</p>
</text>
